<section id="fundulwazi" class="fundulwazi-section" data-aos="fade-up">

    <div class="project-header">

        <div class="project-header-content">

            <span class="section-tag">
                FLAGSHIP PROJECT
            </span>

            <h2>
                FunduLwazi
                <span>AI Document Intelligence</span>
            </h2>

            <p>
                FunduLwazi helps organisations process, understand and
                extract insights from complex business documents using
                Artificial Intelligence, Azure AI and modern cloud
                technologies.
            </p>

            <p>
                <strong>Impact:</strong> In testing, FunduLwazi reduced initial
                document-review time by an average of 89.7% across two
                representative documents, timed manually against baseline
                reading/review time.
            </p>

            <div class="project-links">
                <a href="https://fundulwazi.nolwazintuli.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="visit-link">
                    Visit FunduLwazi →
                </a>

                <button class="story-trigger" @onclick="ToggleStory">
                    Why I built this
                </button>
            </div>

        </div>

    </div>

    @if (showStory)
    {
        <div class="story-overlay" @onclick="ToggleStory">

            <div class="story-modal" @onclick:stopPropagation>

                <button class="close-button" @onclick="ToggleStory" aria-label="Close">
                    ×
                </button>

                <span class="story-label">
                    THE STORY BEHIND FUNDULWAZI
                </span>

                <h3>
                    From observation to solution.
                </h3>

                <p>
                    FunduLwazi wasn't created because I wanted to build an AI
                    application. It started after watching my sister spend
                    countless evenings manually reading, sorting, and
                    processing large volumes of documents.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Instead of immediately writing code, I observed her
                    workflow, asked questions, identified repetitive tasks,
                    and researched how artificial intelligence could reduce
                    that workload.
                </p>

                <p>
                    That experience shaped how I approach every project:
                </p>

                <blockquote class="story-quote">
                    "First, understand the people and the problem, then build
                    technology that genuinely helps them."
                </blockquote>

                <p>
                    That's the version of FunduLwazi I built: one that starts
                    with understanding, not just automation. When I timed it
                    against the manual process my sister used, it cut initial
                    document-review time by an average of 89.7% across two
                    lengthy documents, proof that the observation-first
                    approach translated into something that actually works.
                </p>

            </div>

        </div>
    }

</section>

@code {

    private bool showStory = false;

    private void ToggleStory()

    {

        showStory = !showStory;

    }

}